  "title": "MV era",
  "extends": "lv",
  "inheritTargets": true,
  "dropTargets": ["silicon-gt-not-before-mv", "coil-kanthal-not-before-mv"],
  "note": "MV era per docs/eras/mv.md and its \"Decisions taken\" (which rule): MV drill and greenhouse (16-parallel cap), ore plant (gtceu:ore_plant, type gtceu:ore_processing), bio-refinery (trimmable: WARN if missing), vanadium steel drill bit, GTM's fluid drilling rig (gtceu:mv_fluid_drilling_rig) with fluid veins made infinite by config, and the End, which opens in MV (v0.5.0, DECISIONS 2026-10-24: \"The End moves to MV, with no ilmenite or scheelite\"): the End's key, the eye of ender and blaze drop to MV (docs/journey.md, \"The End's veins\"), the End's ores follow the end-ores rule (a trip with the key; only veins with a sample in the drill's table: veins_end.json without ilmenite, which moves to the Moon, or the scheelite vein, which moves to Mars), the MV drill runs the End's veins with mud, and the End is an MV resource for the era rule. It inherits from LV the world, the machines and ALL the targets (regression), except the two leak checks that stop holding true in MV (GT's silicon and the Kanthal coil). Energy: eu:mv comes from the LV->MV transformer (4 A -> 1 A) on the LV grid, from the MV steam turbine or from combustion generators; eu:hv, from the MV->HV transformer; cables, amperage and batteries aren't modeled. Single-block gtceu:mv_* machines (from the registry) run recipes up to 128 V; electric multiblocks with 2 or more energy hatches of the same tier raise it one step (GTM 7.5.3, WorkableElectricMultiblockMachine.getMaxVoltage): 2 MV hatches = 512 V (HV), which is why the EBF with 2 MV hatches runs the 480 EU/t recipes (stainless steel, Kanthal) that don't fit in a single-block MV machine; the EBF also depends on its coil (cupronickel 1,800 K, Kanthal 2,700 K, +100 K per step above MV). Oil comes from the dump's fluid deposits (fluid_veins.json) that allow the factory's dimension, and is only sustained with worldgen.oreVeins.infiniteBedrockOresFluids = true (config.json). The maintenance hatch is only required with machines.enableMaintenance = true (also config.json). Chromium comes from ruby by electrolysis: the ore plant doesn't process gems and chromite is only in the End. The HV energy hatch is optional (WARN): it needs an HV assembler and a clean room LPIC chip, meaning it already belongs to HV.",

  "contexts": ["minecraft:overworld", "grindless:flat", "grindless:void"],

  "partAbilities": {
    "energy_input": ["gtceu:lv_energy_input_hatch", "gtceu:mv_energy_input_hatch"],
    "energy_output": ["gtceu:lv_energy_output_hatch", "gtceu:mv_energy_output_hatch"],
    "input_bus": ["gtceu:lv_input_bus", "gtceu:ulv_input_bus", "gtceu:mv_input_bus"],
    "output_bus": ["gtceu:lv_output_bus", "gtceu:ulv_output_bus", "gtceu:mv_output_bus"],
    "input_hatch": ["gtceu:lv_input_hatch", "gtceu:ulv_input_hatch", "gtceu:mv_input_hatch"],
    "output_hatch": ["gtceu:lv_output_hatch", "gtceu:ulv_output_hatch", "gtceu:mv_output_hatch"],
    "muffler": ["gtceu:lv_muffler_hatch", "gtceu:ulv_muffler_hatch", "gtceu:mv_muffler_hatch"],
    "maintenance": ["gtceu:maintenance_hatch"]
  },

  "world": [
    {
      "id": "fluid-deposits",
      "mode": "auto",
      "via": ["gtceu:mv_fluid_drilling_rig"],
      "fromFluidVeins": { "fluids": ["gtceu:oil", "gtceu:oil_light", "gtceu:oil_medium", "gtceu:oil_heavy", "gtceu:natural_gas"] },
      "sustainedIf": { "config": "worldgen.oreVeins.infiniteBedrockOresFluids", "equals": true },
      "note": "GTM's fluid drilling rig (decision 2): pumps the chunk's deposit (oil, light/medium/heavy oil, natural gas) and only spends EU. It follows the deposit dump (fluid_veins.json): GTM's filter by dimension (Overworld only), and the pack adds Flat's/Void's (dimensions_fluids.js). Without the infinite-veins config the deposit depletes down to its minimum (WARN). Brine isn't counted: its deposit only occurs in oceans; salt comes from the mixer and electrolysis."
    },
    {
      "id": "end-ores",
      "mode": "manual",
      "bootstrap": true,
      "needs": ["grindless:end_key"],
      "template": "gtceu:raw_{m}",
      "fromVeins": { "dimensions": ["minecraft:the_end"], "requireRecipe": { "type": "gtceu:vein_drilling", "input": "grindless:vein_sample_{id}" } },
      "materials": [],
      "note": "Trip to the End with the key (MV): two ores from each vein the pack offers to the drill (the ones with a sample). The ores come from the live vein registry (veins.json): if the End's bauxite vein started generating ilmenite again, the trip would give it and the ilmenite-not-comes-from-end check would fail. The vein's sample is made from those 2 ores, and after that the MV drill (with mud) keeps them coming."
    }
  ],

